hakios-starlte: the Galaxy S9's device repository for HakiOS (Scion-Project)

This repository is checked out at devices/starlte of Scion-Project/hackios-xnu-kernel. Its LICENSE says
that the device layer under devices/ is under the MIT License. The same terms apply here, by directory:

1. Our own files (the configuration in configs/ and soc/, device.conf, mkimage.sh, the documentation):
   the MIT License below.

2. uefi/files/: changes to Project Silicium's Mu-Silicium (starltePkg). As derived parts, they keep the
   upstream licence, BSD-2-Clause-Patent.

3. prebuilt/: SILICIUM_UEFI.fd and BootShim.bin are built from Mu-Silicium with the changes in uefi/.
   They are under BSD-2-Clause and BSD-2-Clause-Patent, and the UEFI image carries Project Silicium's
   Carbon Hypervisor (GPL-2.0, source at github.com/Project-Silicium/Carbon-Hypervisor).
   mkbootimg.py is AOSP's, under Apache-2.0. prebuilt/README.md has the details.

4. firmware/audio/: Samsung's audio firmware binaries, unchanged (firmware/audio/README.md says where they
   come from). They belong to their owners and are not licensed by this repository.

The kernel drivers this device uses are in the common repository, under its LICENSE (APSL 2.0 for the
kernel). Samsung's GPL-2.0 kernel sources were read for facts (addresses, fields, sequences) and are not
copied here.

